<title>USA: Horry County, S.C., adopts hospitality tax.</title>
<headline>Horry County, S.C., adopts hospitality tax.</headline>
<dateline>CONWAY, S.C. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Carolina's Horry County Council has approved a 2.5 percent hospitality tax to raise money for road construction, county officials said.</p>
<p>Voters rejected the proposed tax last year, but the council approved it 8-3 at a Tuesday night meeting.</p>
<p>The tax applies to hotel rooms, entertainment and restaurant meals.</p>
<p>Revennues are earmarked for road construction and paving projects and for tourism-related expenses.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
